{"case_id":"T5011","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","API protocol","state"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["spng_set_option","spng_get_option","spng_get_unknown_chunks"],"reason":"H0 never calls the new option APIs, so it cannot exercise either validation behavior or the enabled SPNG_KEEP_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS state. This is material because the harness parses attacker-controlled PNG data and calls spng_get_unknown_chunks(), but never enables the option governing whether unknown chunks are kept.","evidence":["S1 adds the public functions spng_set_option() and spng_get_option() and the enum value SPNG_KEEP_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS.","spng_set_option(ctx, SPNG_KEEP_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS, value) normalizes arbitrary values to ctx->keep_unknown = value ? 1 : 0.","spng_get_option() exposes the resulting ctx->keep_unknown state and has distinct error handling for NULL ctx, NULL value, and unsupported option values.","H0 calls spng_get_unknown_chunks(ctx, chunks, &n_chunks) but contains no call to spng_set_option() or spng_get_option()."],"recommended_action":"Extend H0 to derive an option value from fuzz input, call spng_set_option(ctx, SPNG_KEEP_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS, value) before parsing/retrieval, verify it through spng_get_option(), and exercise spng_get_unknown_chunks() in both enabled and disabled states; also cover unsupported option values and safe NULL-argument validation."}
